WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.524 --> 00:00:05.226
Meanwhile, what happened to Edward during Tom's first days as king?

2
00:00:05.266 --> 00:00:06.687
Where did he go when he disappeared?

3
00:00:06.847 --> 00:00:14.751
Edward left the inn with the young man who'd brought the message he said was from Miles.

4
00:00:27.476 --> 00:00:31.258
As they walked toward the bridge and the woods, the man with the eye patch followed them.

5
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.601
But he was careful to keep out of Edward's sight.

6
00:00:39.203 --> 00:00:44.146
After a few minutes of walking in the woods, Edward sat down on a tree stump and refused

7
00:00:44.246 --> 00:00:44.706
to move.

8
00:00:44.726 --> 00:00:49.929
"If Miles wants to talk, he should come to me!"

9
00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:54.352
Edward picked up a stone and gave it an angry toss.

10
00:00:56.436 --> 00:00:57.837
The young man looked surprised.

11
00:00:58.897 --> 00:01:02.399
"You want to sit here and wait while your friend lies wounded?"

12
00:01:02.419 --> 00:01:07.942
"Wounded? You didn't mention that Miles was wounded!"

13
00:01:09.243 --> 00:01:12.084
Edward's attitude instantly changed, and he hopped up.

14
00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:14.065
"We must hurry to him!"

15
00:01:14.086 --> 00:01:16.547
"Not so fast."

16
00:01:17.587 --> 00:01:21.109
The young man, whose name was Frank, studied the bare trees around them.

17
00:01:21.129 --> 00:01:24.251
"What are you looking for?"

18
00:01:24.771 --> 00:01:25.932
Edward said impatiently.

19
00:01:26.892 --> 00:01:28.313
"We have to get going!"

20
00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:31.235
"Aha! There's one!"

21
00:01:32.675 --> 00:01:35.297
Frank pointed to a small rag tied to a branch.

22
00:01:36.718 --> 00:01:38.979
"We need to follow the markers to the old farm."

23
00:01:42.161 --> 00:01:46.563
After a while they came to a clearing with a burned-out house and a ruined barn.

24
00:01:48.044 --> 00:01:49.605
Frank stopped outside the barn.

25
00:01:49.625 --> 00:01:52.787
"Miles! Where are you?"

26
00:01:53.247 --> 00:01:55.068
Edward called, but no one answered.

27
00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.901
He looked around in confusion.

28
00:01:57.921 --> 00:02:00.543
"Something's not right here."

29
00:02:05.306 --> 00:02:08.388
Frank burst into laughter as the man with the eye patch joined them.

30
00:02:08.408 --> 00:02:13.192
"It was almost too easy to trick him," Frank said to the man.

31
00:02:13.212 --> 00:02:15.173
"Who are you?"

32
00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:16.834
Edward asked the man.

33
00:02:16.854 --> 00:02:21.357
"Stop pretending that you don't recognize your own father."

34
00:02:22.218 --> 00:02:24.019
John Canty removed his eye patch.

35
00:02:26.176 --> 00:02:28.557
"You aren't my father," Edward said.

36
00:02:29.517 --> 00:02:33.139
"My father is dead, and I'm King Edward!"

37
00:02:33.159 --> 00:02:37.941
"It's clear that something's wrong with your mind.

38
00:02:39.141 --> 00:02:41.602
I hate to punish you, but if you provoke me, I will."

39
00:02:42.783 --> 00:02:44.444
John shook his fist at Edward.

40
00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:48.245
"Now, where are your mother and sister?

41
00:02:49.085 --> 00:02:51.266
They didn't come to our meeting place on the bridge."

42
00:02:51.286 --> 00:02:55.953
"They're at the palace, of course," Edward said.

43
00:02:59.516 --> 00:03:01.197
John groaned in frustration.

44
00:03:02.758 --> 00:03:05.761
While John and Frank talked, Edward wandered into the barn.

45
00:03:08.563 --> 00:03:12.486
Lying down on a pile of straw, he thought of his dead father and wept.

46
00:03:15.949 --> 00:03:16.910
He was soon asleep.

47
00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:23.696
When Edward woke up, it was dark, and a campfire was burning outside the barn.

48
00:03:25.212 --> 00:03:27.714
Gathered around the fire was a small group of people.

49
00:03:29.115 --> 00:03:32.718
A man tossed away his crutches, laughing about pretending to be lame.

50
00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:40.545
Another man emptied a woman's purse and handed the contents to the group's leader.

51
00:03:40.565 --> 00:03:44.568
"It's a gang of beggars and thieves!"

52
00:03:45.008 --> 00:03:47.210
Edward thought as he watched from inside the barn.

53
00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.432
"They're outlaws!"

54
00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.023
"So, John Canty, what brings you back to your old friends?"

55
00:03:56.564 --> 00:03:57.424
the leader asked.

56
00:03:57.444 --> 00:04:04.129
"Well, Ruffler, I made the mistake of injuring a priest, and now the law is after me," John

57
00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:08.111
said. "I had to flee the city, or they'd throw me in jail."

58
00:04:08.131 --> 00:04:13.555
"You don't want to go to jail," said the man who'd tossed away the crutches.

59
00:04:13.575 --> 00:04:20.600
"I ended up in jail after the king seized my farm to graze his sheep."

60
00:04:22.336 --> 00:04:25.477
The group nodded in agreement as the man continued his story.

61
00:04:26.597 --> 00:04:32.519
"My wife died, and I don't know where my children are—or if they're even alive."

62
00:04:34.759 --> 00:04:36.880
The man struggled to control his emotions.

63
00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.861
"I was sent to jail for stealing food, but I escaped.

64
00:04:44.082 --> 00:04:45.922
If I'm caught, I'll be hanged."

65
00:04:47.823 --> 00:04:49.283
Edward strode out of the barn.

66
00:04:49.303 --> 00:04:54.697
"You will not be hanged, and your land will be returned!

67
00:04:56.258 --> 00:05:00.520
As of today, the cruel reign of my father is over."

68
00:05:02.241 --> 00:05:04.342
There was a murmur of surprise among the group.

69
00:05:04.362 --> 00:05:07.704
"And who are you?"

70
00:05:08.205 --> 00:05:10.466
Ruffler asked.

71
00:05:10.486 --> 00:05:12.307
"I am King Edward!"

72
00:05:16.409 --> 00:05:19.871
A wild burst of laughter met that announcement.

73
00:05:20.391 --> 00:05:21.672
Edward was outraged.

74
00:05:22.504 --> 00:05:24.465
"Is this how you greet your king?"

75
00:05:24.485 --> 00:05:28.806
"Pay no attention to my son," John said.

76
00:05:28.826 --> 00:05:31.907
"He's suffering from a strange illness."

77
00:05:33.527 --> 00:05:34.507
But it was too late.

78
00:05:35.628 --> 00:05:38.729
Some men grabbed Edward and set him on a barrel for a throne.

79
00:05:39.689 --> 00:05:43.670
They crowned him with a tin basin and gave him a ragged blanket for a robe.

80
00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:47.911
"Long live the king!"

81
00:05:48.391 --> 00:05:50.272
the group shouted as they mocked Edward.

82
00:05:53.276 --> 00:05:58.059
As for Miles, he frantically searched all day for Edward but couldn't find the boy.

83
00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.002
Toward evening he gave up and went to an inn.

84
00:06:05.623 --> 00:06:09.465
Eating his supper, Miles thought some more about where Edward might be.

85
00:06:09.485 --> 00:06:14.268
"Edward didn't like the house on Offal Street, so he wouldn't return there.

86
00:06:15.669 --> 00:06:19.631
He's probably headed for my family's home because that's where we were supposed to go."

87
00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:27.147
The next morning Miles started for Hendon Hall, hoping to find Edward along the way.
